    "limits_doc": "I40 round 2 (lead ruling, docs/HUMAN_ANSWERS.md): the only search budget is the sidecar's rlimit per query, counted cumulatively over every check-sat of the query's session from the first check-sat on (holon.smt.run.Session). Registered beside it: memory_max_size_mb, z3's own accounting of the bytes it has allocated, which z3 reads from glibc's malloc (malloc_usable_size), so it is deterministic for this pinned single-threaded binary on the registered glibc, with z3 run in a fixed environment (no malloc tunables or preloads) and with no address-space or data rlimit and no strict overcommit (holon.smt.run.environment_check refuses to run otherwise); an overrun ends the query unknown, named in its reason. e1_rounds_max and hash_rounds_max, BMC's deterministic round caps for lazy E1 and hash concretization (a cap reached ends the query unknown, named in its reason); watchdog_s, a crash guard only: when it fires the run aborts, nothing is recorded and the question stays not run. A solver that ends without an answer is a crash too. No answer depends on wall-clock time, load or an environment variable."
  },
